    title "What are the signs of autism and how does it affect the child?"
    description "Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) is a broad spectrum of atypical behaviors exhibited by impacted individuals. Recognizing the autism signs and seeking a professional diagnosis is key to getting started on the path to a more fulfilling life. Regardless of where a child is on the spectrum, each life matters greatly. Through setting goals in partnership with the family and the primary care physician, Hopebridge utilizes ABA therapy to help each child become his or her best self.&#10;&#10;Learn more about the diagnostic process and program: http://hopebridge.com."
