    title "Autism and Masking webinar"
    description "We were lucky to be joined by the three authors behind the new book Autism and Masking: How and Why People Do It and the Impact It Can Have. Dr Felicity Sedgewick, Dr Laura Hull and Helen Ellis took us through the work that sits behind their book.&#10;&#10;They also helped explain what the main types of masking are and in the Q&#38;A section responded to questions from the live audience on topics as diverse as masking in children to how neurotypical people can support autistic people.&#10;&#10;Introduction: 00:00&#10;Presentation: 2:47&#10;Q&#38;A: 29:52&#10;&#10;Autism and Masking Book: https://www.waterstones.com/book/autism-and-masking/felicity-sedgewick/laura-hull/9781787755796 &#10;Autism and Masking eBook (Kindle): https://amzn.to/3Bdf4BF&#10;&#10;Autistica is the UK&#8217;s leading autism research and campaigning charity. Our vision is a world where every autistic person lives a happy, healthy, long life. Our mission is to enable breakthroughs by working with autistic people, funding research and shaping policy to make more of a difference. &#10;&#10;Learn more about us and connect with us:&#10;&#10;https://www.autistica.org.uk&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/Autistica&#10;Facebook: https://facebook.com/AutisticaCharity&#10;Insta: https://instagram.com/AutisticaUK&#10;Linkedin: https://www.linkedin.com/company/Autistica"
