    id 189
    label "QX7shfjuBe8"
    step 0
    date "2021-07-09T06:21:44Z"
    title "Autism in Girls"
    description "Autism is a field that is constantly learning. While my son was diagnosed at 23 months with autism, my girls did not receive their diagnosis until ages 8 &#38; 11.  For myself, I wasn't diagnosed as autistic until I was 33!  &#10;&#10;The difference in how autism presents in girls is a factor in why so many girls &#38; women have been diagnosed late as most doctors looked for primarily at male symptoms of autism, many of which girls did not have.&#10;&#10;Thankfully, we now know that in addition to the traditional signs of autism, there are things that autistic girls often do that can point towards a correct diagnosis.&#10;&#10;Here are a few ways that autism presents in girls.  For more detailed information, check out: https://www.themomkind.com/autism-symptoms-in-girls/ &#10;&#10;&#10;autism symptoms in girls,autism in women,autism symptoms in women,autistic women,social skills,autism symptoms,autism support,autism information,autism awareness,autism spectrum disorder,autism sypmtoms in girls,autism in girls,female autism,yo samedy sam,asd traits in girls"
