    title "How I use Minecraft to help kids with autism | Stuart Duncan"
    description "The internet can be an ugly place, but you won't find bullies or trolls on Stuart Duncan's Minecraft server, AutCraft. Designed for children with autism and their families, AutCraft creates a safe online environment for play and self-expression for kids who sometimes behave a bit differently than their peers (and who might be singled out elsewhere). Learn more about one of the best places on the internet with this heartwarming talk.&#10;&#10;Check out more TED Talks: http://www.ted.com&#10;&#10;The TED Talks channel features the best talks and performances from the TED Conference, where the world's leading thinkers and doers give the talk of their lives in 18 minutes (or less). Look for talks on Technology, Entertainment and Design -- plus science, business, global issues, the arts and more.&#10;&#10;Follow TED on Twitter: http://www.twitter.com/TEDTalks&#10;Like TED on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/TED&#10;&#10;Subscribe to our channel: https://www.youtube.com/TED"
