    title "Teaching Children with Autism"
    description "MAKE YOUR OWN WHITEBOARD ANIMATIONS. CLICK THE LINK!&#10;http://tidd.ly/69da8562 . &#10;&#10;This is an affiliate link. I earn commission from any sales, so Please Use!&#10;&#10;SUPPORT THIS CHANNEL: &#10;Help keep me going with a tip or contribution&#10;https://paypal.me/frankavella?locale.x=en_US &#10;&#10;TEACHERSPAYTEACHERS STORE&#10;Classroom Posters, Courses, Lessons, Presentations, and More&#10;https://www.teacherspayteachers.com/Store/Teachings-In-Education &#10;&#10;TEESPRING IN EDUCATiON&#10;Stickers, Dress Down Gear, Phone Cases, Coffee Mugs, and More&#10;https://teespring.com/stores/teespring-in-education-2&#10;&#10;FOR PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT &#38; ON-SITE TRAININGS&#10;CONTACT:&#10;midtownavella@gmail.com&#10;&#10;&#10;SOCIAL MEDIA&#10;https://www.linkedin.com/in/frank-avella-404b59b5/ &#10;&#10;https://twitter.com/frank_avella &#10;&#10;This video outlines several strategies that teachers can use to teach students with ASD, autism disorder. The strategies here are outline in a clear fashion with specific examples that educators can use in their classrooms. There are a total of twelve different examples, and each example pertains to a variety of subjects. This video is not just intended for teachers, but also for parents of children with autism. This video is part of a playlist designed to help educators as they continue on their journey. Other videos in the playlist include kwl charts, functional behavioral assessments, classroom management strategies, bloom's taxonomy, lesson planning,  standardized testing for students, and much much more.  Teachers are encouraged to explore this channel and find other videos that can help them with their practices and classroom issues. The channel also tackles larger educational issues such as school choice. Another playlist answers some of the biggest questions that come to mind for educations."
