    title "Author and Autism Advocate Jennifer Cook: What Does It Mean to Be Autistic?"
    description "For Author and Autism Advocate Jennifer Cook, being asked what it means to be autistic is like being asked &#34;what it means to be me.&#34; The hardest part, she says, is &#34;feeling so smart but so stupid at the same time.&#34; That said, she tries to think of herself as different ... so smart &#34;and&#34; anything she wants to be instead of so smart &#34;but&#34; ...&#10;&#10;See our full interview with Jennifer Cook here: https://www.readingrockets.org/teaching/experts/jennifer-cook&#10;&#10;VISIT OUR SISTER SITES&#10;* https://www.adlit.org/ &#8212; information and resources to the parents and educators of struggling adolescent readers and writers&#10;* https://www.colorincolorado.org/ &#8212; a bilingual site for educators and families of English language learners&#10;* https://www.startwithabook.org/ &#8212; engaging ideas for getting kids hooked on learning during the summer&#10;&#10;Don&#8217;t forget to like and subscribe! &#10;Website: https://www.ReadingRockets.org &#10;Donate: https://bit.ly/ReadingRocketsDonation&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/ReadingRockets.org&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/readingrockets"
